[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":111},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news-detail-university-of-maine-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa-281":3},{"news":4,"more":28},{"id":5,"slug":6,"title":7,"content":8,"authorName":9,"authorId":10,"status":11,"recommended":12,"datePosted":13,"deadline":14,"images":15,"notifiedAt":14,"notifiedBy":14,"createdAt":13,"updatedAt":21,"categories":22,"readTime":27},281,"university-of-maine-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa-281","University Of Maine Scholarship 2026: Fully Funded In Usa","\u003Cp>The University of Maine Scholarship covers tuition fees, health insurance, and a living stipend of $31,333 per year until the end of the candidates’ program.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>In this post, the full details of the eligibility, benefits, timeline, and application procedure will be provided.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>University of Maine Scholarship Abstract\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Scholarship Host: University of Maine\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Study Abroad: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarship\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study Abroad\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fcategory\u002Fscholarship\u002Fscholarships-in-usa\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study-In-USA\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Location: USA\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Category: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> ||  \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fpostgraduate-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Postgraduate Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fmasters-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Masters Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fphd-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">PhD Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Tuition\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>$31,333 Living Stipends\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Medical Insurance\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Deadline: June 30, 2026\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>University of Maine Scholarship 2026 Benefits\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>This position provides 2 years of funding for MSc and 3 years for PhD candidates, comprising a 20-hour-per-week assistantship with an annual stipend of $28,000 (MS) or 31,333 (PhD).\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>The University of Maine will cover 65% of health insurance costs and 50% dental insurance costs.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Additional benefits include office space, operational support (including laptop access and travel funds), and an out-of-state tuition waiver.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Responsibilities of the Graduate Assistant\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>The Graduate Assistant will be responsible for:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>developing quantitative economic analyses and applying ecological models to assess forest responses to management practices\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>analyzing long-term inventory plot data and Forest Inventory and Analysis (FIA) data\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>communicating research findings to stakeholders, industry partners, and state-level policymakers.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>The position also involves contributing to peer-reviewed publications and technical reports.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>The student will work closely with an interdisciplinary team at the University of Maine and various key partners in forestry sector in the Northeast US.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>University of Maine Scholarship Requirements\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To be eligible for the  postgraduate University of Maine Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>hold a B.S. degree in Forestry, Economics, Statistics, or a quantitatively focused Environmental or Social \u003Ca class=\"google-anno\" href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship\u002F#\"> \u003Cu>Science\u003C\u002Fu>\u003C\u002Fa> discipline, with a background in natural resource management.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>have a high GPA, strong GRE scores, and solid \u003Ca class=\"google-anno\" href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship\u002F#\"> \u003Cu>scientific\u003C\u002Fu>\u003C\u002Fa> writing and communication skills.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>have experience with statistical analysis, GIS, and programming.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>The ideal candidate will demonstrate proficiency in quantitative analysis, an ability to work independently, a research interest, and a record of scholastic achievement.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Women and minorities are strongly encouraged to apply.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>University of Maine Scholarship 2026 Required Documents\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>While applying for the University of Maine Scholarship 2026, you will be required to submit the following documents;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>A cover letter explaining your interest in the position, your qualifications, and how your interests and skills align with this research project\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>A CV that includes contact information for three references\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>University Transcripts\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>GRE scores\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>How To Apply for University of Maine Scholarship 2026\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To apply for the University of Maine Graduate Assistantship 2026, follow the instructions we have outlined below; \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Read the information we have provided on this webpage and ensure your eligibility\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Prepare the required documents\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Please submit a cover letter explaining your interest in the position, your qualifications, and how your interests and skills align with this research project, a CV that includes contact information for three references, university transcripts, and GRE scores (if available) via this \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fforms.gle\u002Fr5Dr49vP6Ab3q1hc7\">google form\u003C\u002Fa>.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>For more details, please contact:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Dr. Libin T. Louis\u003Cbr \u002F>Assistant Professor of Forestry, University of Maine at Fort Kent\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Graduate Faculty, University of Maine, Orono Email: \u003Ca href=\"mailto:Libin.louis@maine.edu\">Libin.louis@maine.edu\u003C\u002Fa> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>Apply here: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fdocs.google.com\u002Fforms\u002Fd\u002Fe\u002F1FAIpQLSf15cDtfYykT_ZJw-mothAk8hRCJFkpJLuw5ceVZB_H2cC6BA\u002Fviewform\">https:\u002F\u002Fdocs.google.com\u002Fforms\u002Fd\u002Fe\u002F1FAIpQLSf15cDtfYykT_ZJw-mothAk8hRCJFkpJLuw5ceVZB_H2cC6BA\u002Fviewform\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>","Linkskool",16,"published",0,"2026-06-08 11:09:07",null,[16],{"fileName":17,"oldFileName":17,"type":18,"file":19,"url":20},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa\u002F6a2694c3a61f96.22839170_screenshot 2026-06-08 103258.png","image","","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa\u002F6a2694c3a61f96.22839170_screenshot%202026-06-08%20103258.png","2026-06-24 11:55:43",[23],{"id":24,"name":25,"createdAt":26},2,"Opportunities","2026-01-07 13:35:07",3,[29,39,49,58,67,76,85,94,102],{"id":30,"slug":31,"title":32,"images":33,"datePosted":37,"authorName":38},305,"dartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity","Dartmouth College Kings Scholarship Usa 2026: Fully Funded Opportunity",[34],{"fileName":35,"oldFileName":35,"type":18,"file":19,"url":36},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F6a3c3537be16a2.95289717_screenshot 2026-06-24 204255.png","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F6a3c3537be16a2.95289717_screenshot%202026-06-24%20204255.png","2026-06-24 20:51:19","LINKSKOOL",{"id":40,"slug":41,"title":42,"images":43,"datePosted":47,"authorName":48},304,"mexican-government-scholarship-for-foreigners-2026-fully-funded-opportunity","Mexican Government Scholarship For Foreigners 2026: Fully Funded Opportunity",[44],{"fileName":45,"oldFileName":45,"type":18,"file":19,"url":46},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplor